#question(title: [Evaluating Limits], centered: true)[
  - You're trying to guess
    $display(lim_(x -> 0) f(x))$.
  - You plug in $x = 0.1, 0.01, 0.001, ...$
    and get $f(x) = 0$ for all these values.
  - In fact, you're told that for all
    $n = 1, 2, ...$,
    $display(f(1/(10^n)) = 0)$.
  - Can you conclude that
    $display(lim_(x -> 0) f(x) = 0)$?
]
